WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.283
Natalia Panferova compares

00:00:02.095 --> 00:00:03.640
SwiftUI's scroll-driven

00:00:03.451 --> 00:00:04.642
effect APIs

00:00:05.166 --> 00:00:06.309
A Nil Coalescing

00:00:06.121 --> 00:00:06.923
guide to when

00:00:06.734 --> 00:00:08.078
to use scrollTransition

00:00:08.185 --> 00:00:09.128
visualEffect

00:00:09.305 --> 00:00:10.885
onScrollGeometryChange

00:00:10.862 --> 00:00:12.772
and onScrollVisibilityChange

00:00:12.583 --> 00:00:13.703
for effects tied

00:00:13.562 --> 00:00:14.706
to scroll position

00:00:14.517 --> 00:00:15.661
in SwiftUI

00:00:16.198 --> 00:00:17.058
The post shows

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.049
examples of each

00:00:17.979 --> 00:00:18.532
and how to

00:00:18.344 --> 00:00:19.429
choose between them

00:00:19.568 --> 00:00:21.383
SwiftUI provides several

00:00:21.195 --> 00:00:21.997
ways to tie

00:00:21.808 --> 00:00:22.598
the appearance of

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:23.317
content to its

00:00:23.129 --> 00:00:24.166
position as the

00:00:23.978 --> 00:00:25.098
user scrolls

00:00:25.622 --> 00:00:26.801
The scrollTransition

00:00:26.613 --> 00:00:27.909
modifier applies an

00:00:27.721 --> 00:00:28.593
effect to a

00:00:28.405 --> 00:00:29.289
view as it

00:00:29.101 --> 00:00:29.761
enters

00:00:29.797 --> 00:00:30.598
and leaves the

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:31.706
visible region of

00:00:31.518 --> 00:00:32.508
a scroll view

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:34.044
Full story on

00:00:33.855 --> 00:00:34.751
the dashboard
